Apache License, Version 2.0.

Modifications made in this repository
-------------------------------------

1. Go module path
   `github.com/nezhahq/agent` -> `github.com/CyL-Cly/wushang-agent`
   All internal import paths were rewritten accordingly. Third-party
   dependencies under the `github.com/nezhahq/` prefix (go-github-selfupdate,
   service, xsyslog) are external modules and were left unchanged.

2. Self-update feed
   `cmd/agent/main.go` no longer resolves releases from the upstream
   mirror chain (`naibahq/agent` on Gitee, `naiba/nezha-agent` on AtomGit,
   `nezhahq/agent` on GitHub). Self-update is pinned to
   `CyL-Cly/wushang-agent` so an installed agent cannot be silently replaced
   by an upstream binary. The `use_gitee_to_upgrade` and
   `use_atomgit_to_upgrade` configuration keys are still parsed for backwards
   compatibility but no longer influence the update source.

3. CI and repository automation
   Upstream release, AtomGit/Gitee sync, contributors and CodeQL workflows
   were removed. Only `.github/workflows/test.yml` is retained, with the
   cross-repository checkout repointed to `CyL-Cly/wushang-panel`.

4. Documentation
   Project name, README and NOTICE updated to identify this as a
   second-party build.

Binary name left unchanged
--------------------------
The produced binary is still named `nezha-agent` (`.goreleaser.yml`,
`cmd/agent/main.go` and the install scripts all agree on this name, and the
self-update client matches release assets by it). Renaming it would break
self-update asset resolution and existing install scripts, so it was kept as
a functional identifier rather than a branding one.

This is an unofficial build. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by the
Nezha Monitoring project, and changes made here are not contributed back
upstream.
